 to be taking place  in Spain it was a completely arbitrary  setting nothing about the primary story  being told had anything to do with that  locale whereas the city of death setting  it in Paris is actually relevant because  there are plot points involving the  Louvre and the Mona Lisa which is in  Paris so you know it's actually it  actually impacts the story that it's set  in Spain whereas two doctors it was  completely arbitrary which made me hate  that resource allocation went to them  shooting on location in Spain for no  good reason so even though y'all I  complain about it just a tiny bit like  iíve seen location shoot and go way  worse so Wow I'll take it I'll be happy  but ultimately what I love about this is  primarily just the dialogue I and and I  think that's probably where Douglas  Adams had the most influence was the  dialogue and the lines because they are  just so funny I owe the doctor you know  talking to the countess and oh well your  beautiful woman probably and just its  little dust off lines like that that  everywhere what a lovely Butler he's so  violent yes I  Oh like I could seriously I could spend  the next 10 minutes just rattling off  some of the best lines from this and  from this episode and that is is  probably more than anything a big part  of what puts it over the top because  there's a lot to like you it's it's a  pretty tight story all things considered  as it gets towards the end and it gets  into where it's going and how things pan  out and progress and I'll I guess I'll  talk a little bit about spoilers and the  very end I mean I just love this thing  so obviously you've got that so if  you're worried about spoilers this is  probably the point to bow out so if  you're still here in terms of the  realisation that the count and and his  species and their attempts to leave  earth 400 million years ago was actually  what kicked off life that's the sort of  thing that normally I'd be like I don't  know about that but they they give it  proper weight with the doctor point out  that like look your race died so that a  planet could gain new life I'm sorry  that's what happened but dude this is  just the deal and I kind of feel like  there was appropriate weight given to  that and it wasn't it wasn't tossed off  as haphazardly as these sorts of  revelations often are and I think that  that makes it go down better whereas  historically that sort of thing is  something that I don't usually care too  much for so and just seeing you know the  different time displaced versions of  julian glover and the man the mask i  find this very funny and i don't know  why i find this funny here whereas other  times the the alien effects stuff can  can pull me out of it but for some  reason it works for me here I kind of  love the fact that the aliens head  because it's a mask you know worn by I  don't know if they actually put Julian  Glover in that it's a completely head  for a mask that could have used a  stand-in but in any case whoever they  put it on its you know covering their  head so obviously the alien  ed is bigger than a human head and yet  were meant to believe that that is fully  encased within a human mask to create a  normal-sized head and when you know they  like pull it pull the human mask off and  there's the head like that's so much  bigger than the head you just removed  how does that work and that should pull  me up but it does and I find it kind of  adorable and there's just this this  story's just joy to me it's the the ease  and the flow and the chemistry and the  dialogue between you know Tom Baker and  basically everybody he episodes like  this are a big part of why he's my  favorite doctor he's not always in my  favorite stories he doesn't always have  my favorite companions but he I see  episodes like this and see his delivery  in them and I'm like oh I love this guy  god I could I could watch this guy  forever and it's it's just it warms my  heart this this story and I was I was  rea